  "an4.61:13.1": "_Patta_ here is glossed with _yutta_, “fitting”. ",
  "an4.61:13.2": "",
  "an4.61:13.3": "",
  "an4.61:13.4": "",
  "an4.61:13.5": "When the phrase puttadara is resolved, as at SN 3.10, dara is plural. Also note that this kind of context shows that putta is by default “children” and should be translated as “son” only when required by the context. ",
  "an4.61:13.6": "",
  "an4.61:13.7": "_ṭhānagata_ is \"what has gone for a reason\". _Pattagata_ is similar, what has been spent in a worthy manner. ayatanaso is “within means or scope”. ",
